{
  "id": "hogflowschedule-status-and-sync-with-flow-batch-job-state",
  "title": "HogFlowSchedule status and sync with flow/batch job state",
  "kind": "invariant",
  "answers": [
    "What schedule state must stay in sync with flow status?",
    "How do schedule statuses change?",
    "What happens when a schedule RRULE is edited?",
    "What are batch job states?"
  ],
  "body": "- `HogFlowSchedule.Status` = active|paused|completed (backend/models/hog_flow_schedule/hog_flow_schedule.py); SCHEDULED_TRIGGER_TYPES=(\"batch\",\"schedule\").\n- `completed` is set only by the scheduler when RRULE is exhausted (`internal_process_due_schedules.advance_next_run`); scheduler also applies the active-flow gate.\n- `paused` set by `_pause_schedules_on_audience_change` in hog_flow.py.\n- `HogFlowScheduleSerializer.update` resets next_run_at=None when rrule/starts_at/timezone change and reactivates unless paused (so completed→active on edited RRULE). `validate` requires valid RRULE, future occurrences, at most hourly.\n- Schedule create for agent sources on batch trigger requires active flow + confirm token (`schedules` POST).\n- Batch job `HogFlowBatchJob.State` = waiting|queued|active|completed|cancelled|failed; new jobs start queued; workers advance; Django only sets cancelled.\n- Frontend: `workflowLogic` reloads schedules and `setSchedules` on save success; `pendingSchedule` written in saveWorkflowSuccess.",
  "applies": "internal_process_due_schedules was cited from the agent's summary, not read directly.",
